// Flat merge of the salam/semantic port (see salam/PORTING.md "Layout - FLAT"):
// compiler/src/semantic/ - one package `semantic`, one file. Import alias for
// consumers: `sm`. Because the checker functions are mutually recursive, the
// module is ported by four sequential agents INTO THIS ONE FILE:
//
//   5a (DONE): sema_internal.h (state struct + helpers), types.h/types.c,
//       symbol.h/symbol.c, sema_util.c, sema_type.c, builtins.h/builtins.c.
//   5b (DONE): sema.c + sema_order.c + sema_decl.c (run/collect/imports/
//       packages/prelude/ordering/unused checks/xml).
//   5c (DONE): sema_generic.c, sema_expr.c, sema_call.c, sema_lit.c,
//       sema_fold.c + the lvalue/pure-write slice of sema_stmt.c
//       (analyze_lvalue/sema_classify_write/sema_check_pure_write).
//   5d (DONE): the rest of sema_stmt.c (blocks/statements/var decls/
//       terminators/E062 unused params), sema_match.c, sema_layout.c (plus
//       the layout registry/schema slice it validates against), dce.c.
//
// >>> The port is COMPLETE - no stubs remain. New private functions go
// >>> before the "PUBLIC API" section (rule E088: pub funcs come last).
//
// C -> Salam decisions for this module (later stages must inherit these):
// - type_t* -> `pub type TypeId = int`, an index into Sema.types.
//   The 18 primitive types are pre-seeded at ids 0..TY_F64, so for
//   primitives TypeId == TY_* kind value (mirrors type_ctx_t.prims[]).
//   The C NULL type pointer is TYPE_NONE (= -1), NOT 0 (0 is the TY_ERROR
//   primitive; C distinguishes "<null>" from "<error>" and NULL checks).
// - scope_t* / symbol_t* / func_sig_t* -> ScopeId / SymId / SigId indices
//   into Sema.scopes / Sema.syms / Sema.sigs; slot 0 is a sentinel = C NULL
//   (same convention as ast.NodeId).
// - ast_node_t* -> at.NodeId int (0 = none). The Ast is NOT stored inside
//   Sema (Vector-header copy hazard); it is threaded as `a &: at.Ast`
//   through every function that touches nodes, like the parser port.
// - type_ctx_t / sema_t are merged into ONE `pub struct Sema` (the C tc was
//   a field of sema_t anyway). No globals except the const data tables
//   (k_sm_*; repo-unique names per PORTING.md).
// - Renamed fields (Salam keywords): type_t.kind..params keep C names;
//   symbol_t.type -> Symbol.ty; func_sig_t.ret -> Sig.ret_type;
//   scope_t.func -> Scope.fn; sema_t.cc -> Sema.cctab (import-alias clash).
// - scope_t's lazy hash index (hindex/hcap, symbol.c) is dropped: lookup is
//   a linear scan with identical semantics (perf-only difference).
// - lambda_ctx_t linked list (prev) -> Vector<LambdaCtx> stack Sema.lam.
// - sema_t.pkg_cache (vec of [path, symbol] pairs) -> two parallel vectors
//   pkg_cache_paths / pkg_cache_syms.
// - s->match_yield_collect (vec_t* into a caller's local) -> the vector
//   match_yield_collect + bool match_yield_active on Sema.
// - SERR/SWARN macros -> serr()/swarn() below; messages are pre-formatted at
//   the call site with co.FormatN(i18.Tr(fmt), ...) (the C diag_report did
//   the i18n_tr internally; the diag port takes a final message body).
// - type_to_string/mangle_func: the C clamps output at fixed char buffers
//   (128/160/256/512 bytes); not replicated - only pathological giant nested
//   types would differ.
// 5b (DONE): sema.c + sema_order.c + sema_decl.c are ported. Notes:
// - the C static globals g_stdlib_root / g_seg_aliases[512] are the g_sm_* module
//   globals below; get_exe_dir derives from os.Args()[0] (the C read
//   /proc/self/exe) and SALAM_STDLIB_PREFIX (a configure-time #define) has
//   no port equivalent - SALAM_STD / salam.cfg / exe-relative paths cover it.
// - RunCached's shared_pkg_cache cannot cross Sema instances (SymIds are
//   Sema-local); the package cache is Sema-owned (pkg_cache_paths/syms).
// - imported package files are lexed/parsed into the SAME at.Ast that holds
//   the main program (the C used one arena; NodeIds stay tree-unique).
// 5c (DONE): sema_generic.c + sema_expr.c + sema_call.c + sema_lit.c +
// sema_fold.c are ported, plus sema_stmt.c's lvalue classification and
// pure-write check (AST_INCDEC needed them - 5d must NOT port them again).
// Notes for 5d:
// - generic_template gained an `a &: at.Ast` param (the C read
//   sym->decl->typarams directly; the port needs the tree).
// - g_subst does NOT share the clone's list/dims vectors (the C did); it
//   copies the child NodeIds into fresh vectors so FreeAst frees each
//   vector exactly once.
// - sema_collect / sema_check_pass iterate the program with LIVE
//   at.Child/ChildCount reads: g_instantiate_struct/-func APPEND synthetic
//   instances to s.program's list mid-iteration, and a snapshot Vector
//   header would dangle on realloc. Keep any new program-list loops live.
// - check_lambda builds its inference Sig as a real Sema-owned s.sigs slot
//   (the C used a stack func_sig_t); the slot simply stays allocated.
// - global `const N := 2*3` is NOT usable as an array dim even in the C
//   (collect resolves field types before the initializer folds; only
//   literal-initialized consts carry ival there). Local consts get their
//   ival from the folded initializer in check_stmt (5d).
// 5d (DONE): sema_stmt.c remainder + sema_match.c + sema_layout.c + dce.c.
// - dce.c state -> g_sm_dce_* globals (DceReset/Enable/Finish/Reachable…);
//   dce_note gained an `a &: at.Ast` param (dce_caller_rooted reads the
//   current function's decl node). Disabled by default, like the C.
// - sema_layout.c needs the layout registry: the registry.c/schema.c slice
//   it reads (elem/attr/value tables, layout_schema_init, value validators,
//   layout_localize_names) is ported HERE as g_sm_lay_* + lay_*/schema_*
//   private funcs; pub LayoutSchemaInit(root) replaces the driver's
//   layout_schema_init call - callers of Run that check layout blocks must
//   invoke it once (the tests and tests_port/sema_run.salam do).
// - sema_check_match: the C per-arm heap vec of match_yield_t and the
//   arm_yields vec-of-vecs are flattened into parallel vectors with
//   per-arm [offset,count) windows; s.match_yield_collect is swapped
//   per-arm exactly like the C pointer (match_yield_active = "collect is
//   non-NULL"). Exhaustiveness messages replicate sal_catf's 256-byte
//   clamping byte-for-byte (sm_catf256).
// - Corpus gate: tests_port/sema_run.salam mirrors the driver's
//   `--emit-symbol-xml` pipeline; symbol XML + rc byte-identical to HEAD
//   bin/salam across compiler/tests (see PORTING.md for numbers). stderr
//   matches after stripping logger lines and code-less lexer/parser render
//   blocks (the logger port's rich diag path is unwired; LogAt carries no
//   span length - note for the driver/logger wave).
package semantic

import str
import os
import co "sal_core.salam"
import tok "token.salam"
import at "ast.salam"
import lg "logger.salam"
import dg "diag.salam"
import i18 "i18n.salam"
import cc "condcomp.salam"
import lp "langpack.salam"
import src "source.salam"
import lx "lexer.salam"
import ps "parser.salam"
import x "xml.salam"

